$x^{\ln \left(\frac{y}{z}\right)} \cdot y^{\ln (x z)^2} \cdot z^{\ln \left(\frac{x}{y}\right)}=y^{4 \ln y}\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow \ln \left[x^{\ln \left(\frac{y}{z}\right)}\right]+\ln \left[y^{\ln (x z)^2}\right]+\ln \left[z^{\ln \left(\frac{x}{y}\right)}\right]=\ln \left[y^{4 \ln y}\right] \\
& \Rightarrow\left[\ln \left(\frac{y}{z}\right) \ln x\right]+[2 \ln (x z) \ln y]+\left[\ln \left(\frac{x}{y}\right) \ln z\right]=4[\ln y]^2 \\
& \Rightarrow \ln \mathrm{x}[\ln \mathrm{y}-\ln \mathrm{z}]+2 \ln \mathrm{y}[\ln \mathrm{x}+\ln \mathrm{z}] \\
& +\ln \mathrm{z}[\ln \mathrm{x}-\ln \mathrm{y}]=4[\ln \mathrm{y}]^2
\end{aligned}\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow 3 \ln x+\ln \mathrm{z}=4 \ln \mathrm{y} \\
& \Rightarrow \frac{\ln \mathrm{x}+\ln \mathrm{x}+\ln \mathrm{x}+\ln \mathrm{z}}{4}=\ln \mathrm{y}
\end{aligned}\therefore \quad \ln y$ is the $A M of \ln x, \ln x, \ln x, \ln x \ \text{ and } \ln z$.

